{'GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_WORLDPOP': {'GEO_OPENSTREETMAP': ['HISTORY_CHANGESETS', 'HISTORY_NODES', 'PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS', 'PLANET_FEATURES', 'PLANET_NODES', 'PLANET_RELATIONS', 'HISTORY_LAYERS', 'HISTORY_RELATIONS', 'PLANET_WAYS', 'PLANET_LAYERS'], 'WORLDPOP': ['POPULATION_GRID_1KM']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• WORLDPOP.POPULATION_GRID_1KM  
  – "alpha_3_code": filter grid cells that belong to Singapore (‘SGP’).  
  – "last_updated": keep only the most‑recent population layer that is **before 2023‑01‑01**.  
  – "longitude_centroid", "latitude_centroid": build a GEOGRAPHY point for every 1 km grid cell centroid (ST_POINT) – later used for ST_CONVEXHULL and ST_DISTANCE.  
  – "population": population value that must finally be returned for the grid cell farthest from a hospital.  
  – "geo_id": stable identifier to keep the link to each grid cell.  
  – "geog": polygon of the grid cell (can also be used for distance / intersects tests).  

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_LAYERS  
  – "layer_code": select hospitals (2110 = hospital, 2120 = doctors/clinics).  
  – "geometry": geometry of every OSM feature – used with ST_INTERSECTS and ST_DISTANCE.  
  – "osm_timestamp": guarantee the feature existed before 2023‑01‑01 (≤ 1672444800000000 µs).  

Conditions that will be needed  
1. POPULATION_GRID_1KM."alpha_3_code" = 'SGP'  
2. POPULATION_GRID_1KM."last_updated" < DATE '2023‑01‑01' (and choose max date).  
3. PLANET_LAYERS."layer_code" IN (2110, 2120)  
4. PLANET_LAYERS."osm_timestamp" ≤ 1672444800000000  
5. ST_INTERSECTS(PLANET_LAYERS."geometry", <convexHull_of_all_Singapore_grid_centroids>)  
6. Distance calculated with ST_DISTANCE between every grid‑centroid point and every hospital geometry.  
